      "updated": 1790779062003,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "class Grid[T](ABS, Callable):\n# Check if possible to inherit from list of lists?\n# With the Grid class, we should be able to:\n    1. Checking neighbours and being able to\n        access each of its cells.\n    2. Return a row or column.\n---------------------------------------------\n_factory: Callable[T] | Iterable? | Container?\n_grid: list[list[T]]\n---------------------------------------------\n+ __init__(self, cell_factory: callable = Cell,\n     width: int, height: int, default_value: T)\n+ row(): Iterator[T]\n+ column(): Iterator[T]\n+ property(valid): bool\n    ...\nproperty(cell: Type[Cell[T]])\n+ __getitem__(self, y) -> list[T]\n+ __iter__(self) -> Iterator",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "WWGztZaqtw-9E-TZuScvU",
      "originalText": "class Grid[T](ABS, Callable):\n# Check if possible to inherit from list of lists?\n# With the Grid class, we should be able to:\n    1. Checking neighbours and being able to\n        access each of its cells.\n    2. Return a row or column.\n---------------------------------------------\n_factory: Callable[T] | Iterable? | Container?\n_grid: list[list[T]]\n---------------------------------------------\n+ __init__(self, cell_factory: callable = Cell,\n     width: int, height: int, default_value: T)\n+ row(): Iterator[T]\n+ column(): Iterator[T]\n+ property(valid): bool\n    ...\nproperty(cell: Type[Cell[T]])\n+ __getitem__(self, y) -> list[T]\n+ __iter__(self) -> Iterator",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
