      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790779463068,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "class Room(Cell[T]) \nWill use most of the \ndefault implementation of Cell[T]\nWill add property(surrounded), break_wall()\n-------------------------------------------------\nmagic_property based on T name here? (i.e walls)\n-------------------------------------------------\n+ property(valid): bool\n+ __init__(self, _grid: Grid[T])\n+ __call__(self, y: int, x: int) -> self\n+ __iter__(self): Iterator[T]\n+ property(surrounded): list[T]\n+ neighbour(self, m: Move) -> Cell[T]",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "8mYjum0sH1zW4I4mMr-YK",
      "originalText": "class Room(Cell[T]) \nWill use most of the \ndefault implementation of Cell[T]\nWill add property(surrounded), break_wall()\n-------------------------------------------------\nmagic_property based on T name here? (i.e walls)\n-------------------------------------------------\n+ property(valid): bool\n+ __init__(self, _grid: Grid[T])\n+ __call__(self, y: int, x: int) -> self\n+ __iter__(self): Iterator[T]\n+ property(surrounded): list[T]\n+ neighbour(self, m: Move) -> Cell[T]",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
